      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T08:33:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I reproduced this with the installed clang-tidy/LLVM 14.0.0:\n\nvalid: 0\nerror: repetition-operator operand invalid\n\nThe test constructs llvm::Regex(\"(?!^subprojects).*\") and calls isValid(). clang-tidy uses llvm::Regex for HeaderFilterRegex (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/clang-tools-extra/clang-tidy/ClangTidyDiagnosticConsumer.cpp), and LLVM documents that this defaults to POSIX ERE syntax (https://llvm.org/doxygen/classllvm_1_1Regex.html). POSIX ERE does not support the negative look-ahead (?!...), so this filter is invalid.",
      "parentUuid": "497a9992_8317e42a",
      "revId": "4407d7e6f2f940df4775c4bdc95f9125aad0623b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
