      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T13:18:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I reproduced the actual filtering behavior with clang-tidy-23.\n\nWith a header containing `int *pointer \u003d 0;` and a valid filter:\n\n$ clang-tidy-23 main.cpp --checks\u003d\u0027-*,modernize-use-nullptr\u0027 \\\n    --header-filter\u003d\u0027.*\u0027 -- -std\u003dc++17 -I.\n\n.../include/issue.hpp:4:20: warning: use nullptr [modernize-use-nullptr]\n\nWith the proposed filter:\n\n$ clang-tidy-23 main.cpp --checks\u003d\u0027-*,modernize-use-nullptr\u0027 \\\n    --header-filter\u003d\u0027(?!^subprojects).*\u0027 -- -std\u003dc++17 -I.\n\n1 warning generated.\nSuppressed 1 warnings (1 in non-user code).\n\nSo clang-tidy produces the header diagnostic, but this pattern does not match the header and suppresses it. This is consistent with `HeaderFilterRegex` using `llvm::Regex`, whose default syntax is POSIX ERE and does not support `(?!...)` look-ahead.",
      "parentUuid": "1c0739d5_29d444b1",
      "revId": "4407d7e6f2f940df4775c4bdc95f9125aad0623b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
